# CODEOWNERS.addition
#
# These two lines must be APPENDED to the end of .github/CODEOWNERS
# (after the existing entries) when promoting the security-audit action.
#
# SYNTAX NOTE (PM-010 fix): GitHub CODEOWNERS uses gitignore-style glob patterns.
# The period in '.github/' is a LITERAL character — no backslash escaping needed
# or valid. The live .github/CODEOWNERS uses the same unescaped style (e.g.,
# .github/workflows/, .github/dependabot.yml). Using \.github/ would be incorrect
# and GitHub may silently ignore the pattern, leaving the paths unprotected.
#
# To deploy: open .github/CODEOWNERS and append the two lines below the existing
# '.context/rules/' and 'docs/governance/' entries. Owner handle matches the
# existing CODEOWNERS entries in this repo.

# Composite action and accept-list files — changes require maintainer review
# to prevent supply-chain attacks via the action script or CVE suppression abuse.
.github/actions/   @geekatron
.github/security/  @geekatron
